  "identityStatus": "Whole curved Ataturk rock-fill barrier and mapped crest road,eight exposed penstocks with intake headwall and lower saddles,long native-plan powerhouse and adjacent control house,and the separate eastern gated spillway with broad divided chute and stilling-basin retaining walls. Independent terraced hills,roads,settlement,transmission infrastructure and river islands remain native context. Static closed gates;no lettering,logos,people,vehicles or fluid simulation. One common Y=0 reference equals the standard viewer reservoir sample at local[0,-700],530m. Estimated crest+14m and foundation-155m retain the169m height fact as an overall illustrative envelope,not a surveyed crest/base pair. Tailwater-143m,hall floor-130m,12m hall height,13m control-house height,penstock paths and spillway profile are picture-scale interpretations. No independent component terrain snapping or surrounding field flattening.",
